content.text:
Read and follow `skills/pac-grill-with-docs/SKILL.md`.

**Provided arguments**: 
https://github.com/ladislas/mypac/issues/447

The v1 scope is fixed: pac-deep-read, pac-grill-me, pac-zoom-out, and pac-explore.

Refine the implementation design for exporting those four workflows as ChatGPT / Agent Skills.

Audit each canonical SKILL.md and its relevant Pi prompt where one exists. Determine the minimum runtime-neutral cleanup required while preserving existing Pi behavior.

Settle explicitly:
- which frontmatter fields are portable, Pi-specific, or unnecessary, especially compatibility and disable-model-invocation;
- whether any of the four skills contain Pi-only routing, tools, filesystem assumptions, slash-command references, or references outside their skill directory;
- whether reusable behavior currently living in a prompt should move into the canonical skill, keeping Pi prompts thin;
- the smallest explicit export allowlist/manifest representation;
- the exact export command and deterministic per-skill archive layout;
- how portability should be enforced so a future Pi-specific dependency causes validation to fail rather than being rewritten;
- which Agent Skills validator should be used and whether it is reliable enough for the normal test gate.

Use pac-deep-read as the reference portable skill/prompt pattern.

Inspect pac-to-prd only as a non-blocking comparison case. Do not expand v1 to include it unless portability is essentially free.

Do not design a semantic transpiler, parallel ChatGPT-specific skill tree, generic cross-agent framework, or bulk-install mechanism.

Record the resulting decisions and smallest implementation plan durably on #447 so the next step can be /pac-lwot.

